our imagination.

12
00:00:36,129 --> 00:00:39,781
Most of the world's fresh water is frozen. Around

13
00:00:39,781 --> 00:00:42,836
two thirds of it is locked in ice, mostly

14
00:00:42,836 --> 00:00:46,561
in two giant ice sheets: Antarctica and Greenland.

15
00:00:47,111 --> 00:00:50,747
The Antarctic ice sheet is enormous. In places it's

16
00:00:50,747 --> 00:00:54,312
more than four kilometers thick. If it all melted,

17
00:00:54,312 --> 00:00:58,162
it would raise sea levels by about fifty-eight meters.

18
00:00:58,712 --> 00:01:02,172
Most of that ice sits in East Antarctica, which

19
00:01:02,172 --> 00:01:05,632
is mostly on high ground and fairly stable. The

20
00:01:05,632 --> 00:01:09,312
bigger worry is West Antarctica, where much of the

21
00:01:09,312 --> 00:01:12,404
ice rests on rock below sea level, so warm

22
00:01:12,404 --> 00:01:15,864
ocean water can eat away at it from underneath.

23
00:01:16,414 --> 00:01:20,197
Greenland's ice would add about seven meters more. And

24
00:01:20,197 --> 00:01:23,630
all the mountain glaciers in the Alps, the Andes,

25
00:01:23,630 --> 00:01:27,343
the Himalayas and Alaska together would add less than

26
00:01:27,343 --> 00:01:28,254
half a meter.

27
00:01:28,804 --> 00:01:31,233
Add it up, and if every bit of land

28
00:01:31,233 --> 00:01:34,842
ice melted, the oceans would rise by roughly seventy

29
00:01:34,842 --> 00:01:38,937
meters. That's about the height of a twenty-story building.

30
00:01:39,487 --> 00:01:42,919
Where would all that water go? The oceans already

31
00:01:42,919 --> 00:01:47,051
cover about seventy-one percent of the planet. With seventy

32
00:01:47,051 --> 00:01:50,412
more meters, they would swallow many of the low,

33
00:01:50,412 --> 00:01:54,194
flat places where people prefer to live: river deltas,

34
00:01:54,194 --> 00:01:56,085
coastal plains and islands.

35
00:01:56,635 --> 00:02:00,109
About forty percent of the world's people live within

36
00:02:00,109 --> 00:02:03,321
one hundred kilometers of the coast, which is why

37
00:02:03,321 --> 00:02:05,616
sea level matters to so many of us.

38
00:02:06,166 --> 00:02:10,318
One important detail: melting sea ice, like the floating

39
00:02:10,318 --> 00:02:13,877
ice at the North Pole, doesn't raise sea levels,

40
00:02:13,877 --> 00:02:17,659
just like melting ice cubes don't overflow a glass.

41
00:02:17,659 --> 00:02:19,883
It's ice on land that matters.

42
00:02:20,433 --> 00:02:23,556
Quick question. Do you live near the coast? How

43
00:02:23,556 --> 00:02:26,346
high above sea level is your home? Tell me

44
00:02:26,346 --> 00:02:27,409
in the comments.

45
00:02:27,959 --> 00:02:31,846
So, seventy meters of extra ocean. Let's redraw the

46
00:02:31,846 --> 00:02:35,885
map, starting with North America. The entire state of

47
00:02:35,885 --> 00:02:40,305
Florida would vanish under the Atlantic, along with Miami,

48
00:02:40,305 --> 00:02:41,677
Tampa and Orlando.

49
00:02:42,227 --> 00:02:45,874
Along the Gulf of Mexico, Houston and New Orleans

50
00:02:45,874 --> 00:02:49,522
would be underwater. On the East Coast, New York,

51
00:02:49,522 --> 00:02:52,723
Washington and Boston would be mostly lost.

52
00:02:53,273 --> 00:02:57,024
In Mexico, much of the low, flat Yucatán Peninsula

53
00:02:57,024 --> 00:03:01,451
would be flooded, including Cancún and Mérida. Veracruz and

54
00:03:01,451 --> 00:03:05,878
other coastal cities would disappear. But Mexico City, more

55
00:03:05,878 --> 00:03:09,555
than two thousand two hundred meters up, would be

56
00:03:09,555 --> 00:03:10,681
perfectly safe.

57
00:03:11,231 --> 00:03:14,725
In South America, the Amazon basin is so low

58
00:03:14,725 --> 00:03:18,617
and flat that the Atlantic would push far inland,

59
00:03:18,617 --> 00:03:21,953
turning much of it into a huge inland sea.

60
00:03:21,953 --> 00:03:25,289
Buenos Aires and Montevideo would be gone.

61
00:03:25,839 --> 00:03:30,151
In Europe, London, Venice and Amsterdam would be underwater.

62
00:03:30,151 --> 00:03:34,607
The Netherlands and Denmark would almost completely disappear.

63
00:03:35,157 --> 00:03:38,838
In Asia, Bangladesh, home to more than one hundred

64
00:03:38,838 --> 00:03:43,476
seventy million people, would be almost entirely flooded, along

65
00:03:43,476 --> 00:03:47,083
with Shanghai, Bangkok and much of coastal China.

66
00:03:47,633 --> 00:03:51,021
Australia would get a new inland sea, as the

67
00:03:51,021 --> 00:03:54,794
ocean poured into its low interior basins. And in

68
00:03:54,794 --> 00:03:59,414
Africa, the least affected continent, Alexandria and much of

69
00:03:59,414 --> 00:04:02,417
Egypt's Nile Delta would still be lost.

70
00:04:02,967 --> 00:04:07,472
Some countries wouldn't need seventy meters to vanish. Island

71
00:04:07,472 --> 00:04:11,681
nations like the Maldives, Kiribati and Tuvalu are mostly

72
00:04:11,681 --> 00:04:14,857
only a couple of meters above the sea. Even

73
