a small rise threatens their future.

74
00:04:18,066 --> 00:04:20,616
Which city would you miss the most? Tell me

75
00:04:20,616 --> 00:04:21,565
in the comments.

76
00:04:22,115 --> 00:04:25,861
The ocean wouldn't be the only change. Ice reflects

77
00:04:25,861 --> 00:04:29,608
sunlight back to space. Without it, darker land and

78
00:04:29,608 --> 00:04:33,502
ocean would absorb more heat, warming the planet even

79
00:04:33,502 --> 00:04:33,869
more.

80
00:04:34,419 --> 00:04:38,189
Billions of people in Asia and South America depend

81
00:04:38,189 --> 00:04:41,662
on mountain glaciers for river water in the dry

82
00:04:41,662 --> 00:04:45,580
season. Without them, rivers fed by the Himalayas and

83
00:04:45,580 --> 00:04:47,945
Andes could shrink dramatically.

84
00:04:48,495 --> 00:04:51,808
Has Earth ever had no ice? Yes. Around fifty

85
00:04:51,808 --> 00:04:55,346
million years ago, there were no big ice sheets

86
00:04:55,346 --> 00:04:58,659
at all. The planet was much warmer, and palm

87
00:04:58,659 --> 00:05:02,575
trees and crocodile relatives lived near the Arctic.

88
00:05:03,125 --> 00:05:06,992
And something surprising would happen to the land. Ice

89
00:05:06,992 --> 00:05:10,072
is so heavy that it pushes the ground down.

90
00:05:10,072 --> 00:05:14,298
Without it, Greenland and Antarctica would slowly rise back

91
00:05:14,298 --> 00:05:17,951
up, by hundreds of meters, over thousands of years.

92
00:05:18,501 --> 00:05:22,040
We'd also lose a library. Ice cores drilled from

93
00:05:22,040 --> 00:05:25,505
Antarctica hold tiny bubbles of air from as far

94
00:05:25,505 --> 00:05:29,191
back as eight hundred thousand years ago, a record

95
00:05:29,191 --> 00:05:30,960
of Earth's past climate.

96
00:05:31,510 --> 00:05:35,678
Now the most important question. Is this actually going

97
00:05:35,678 --> 00:05:39,315
to happen? Not anytime soon. Melting all the ice

98
00:05:39,315 --> 00:05:42,876
on Earth would take thousands of years, even in

99
00:05:42,876 --> 00:05:45,377
the worst-case warming scenarios.

100
00:05:45,927 --> 00:05:49,887
But the ice is melting faster than before. Satellites

101
00:05:49,887 --> 00:05:53,923
show Greenland has been losing, on average, around two

102
00:05:53,923 --> 00:05:57,286
hundred seventy billion tons of ice a year in

103
00:05:57,286 --> 00:05:58,407
recent decades.

104
00:05:58,957 --> 00:06:03,280
Sea levels have already risen more than twenty centimeters

105
00:06:03,280 --> 00:06:06,782
since 1900, and the rate is speeding up. Today,

106
00:06:06,782 --> 00:06:10,733
the ocean rises by about four millimeters every year.

107
00:06:11,283 --> 00:06:16,022
Mountain glaciers are shrinking fastest of all. In Mexico,

108
00:06:16,022 --> 00:06:20,761
glaciers on Iztaccíhuatl have almost vanished, and in 2024

109
00:06:20,761 --> 00:06:25,746
scientists said Venezuela had become the first Andean country

110
00:06:25,746 --> 00:06:29,096
in modern times to lose all its glaciers.

111
00:06:29,646 --> 00:06:35,112
In Antarctica, scientists are closely watching Thwaites Glacier, nicknamed

112
00:06:35,112 --> 00:06:39,027
the Doomsday Glacier. It's about the size of Florida,

113
00:06:39,027 --> 00:06:41,761
and on its own it holds enough ice to

114
00:06:41,761 --> 00:06:45,454
raise sea levels by around sixty-five centimeters.

115
00:06:46,004 --> 00:06:50,433
The UN's climate scientists project that by 2100, seas

116
00:06:50,433 --> 00:06:54,861
could rise by roughly thirty centimeters to around one

117
00:06:54,861 --> 00:06:59,290
meter, depending largely on how much greenhouse gas we

118
00:06:59,290 --> 00:06:59,700
emit.

119
00:07:00,250 --> 00:07:03,953
Even one meter would matter. Hundreds of millions of

120
00:07:03,953 --> 00:07:07,443
people live in low coastal areas, and higher seas

121
00:07:07,443 --> 00:07:09,509
make storm floods much worse.

122
00:07:10,059 --> 00:07:14,118
People are adapting. The Netherlands, with about a quarter

123
00:07:14,118 --> 00:07:17,478
of its land below sea level, has defended itself

124
00:07:17,478 --> 00:07:21,537
with dikes and storm barriers for centuries. Venice raised

125
00:07:21,537 --> 00:07:24,966
its MOSE flood gates. And Indonesia is building a

126
00:07:24,966 --> 00:07:28,256
new capital, partly because Jakarta is sinking.

127
00:07:28,806 --> 00:07:31,570
So, what if all the ice on Earth melted?

128
00:07:31,570 --> 00:07:35,300
The map would change completely, and the world's great

129
00:07:35,300 --> 00:07:38,617
coastal cities would be lost. It won't happen in

130
00:07:38,617 --> 00:07:41,449
our lifetime. But how much ice we keep is

131
00:07:41,449 --> 00:07:43,867
